      "description": "Watch Crystal Palace vs Lech Poznan highlights and goals from UEFA Europa League on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on September 17, 2026. The atmosphere under the lights on September 17, 2026 , promised a memorable night of football as the group stages of the UEFA Europa League got underway. Crystal Palace played host to Lech Poznań , with both sides eager to make an immediate impact in their continental campaign. First Half Dominance Crystal Palace wasted no time in asserting their dominance on home soil. Just 10 minutes into the match, the stadium erupted as Yeremy Pino found the back of the net to give the hosts an early lead. The pressure from the South London side remained relentless, and they were rewarded again in the 27th minute. Adam Wharton turned provider, delivering a pinpoint ball to Chris Richards , who clinicaly doubled the advantage. The visitors struggled to contain the wave of attacks, and things went from bad to worse in the 34th minute. After a foul in the box, the referee pointed to the spot, and Joergen Strand Larsen stepped up to calmly dispatch the penalty. With a three-goal cushion before the break, the \"Eagles\" looked firmly in control of the contest. Late Drama and the Final Blow The second half saw a series of tactical changes as both managers looked to influence the game's flow. Crystal Palace introduced fresh legs in the form of Dwight McNeil and Edward Nketiah , maintaining their high tempo. Lech Poznań attempted to fight back, but their task became nearly impossible in the 88th minute when Radoslaw Murawski was shown a second yellow card and subsequently sent off. Capitalizing on the numerical advantage almost immediately, the hosts added one final flourish to the scoreline. In the 89th minute, McNeil showcased his creative quality by setting up Nketiah , who fired home to seal a comprehensive victory. It was a perfect start for the English side, leaving the visitors with plenty to ponder as the referee blew the final whistle at 90+4'."
